{"id":"paid-after-end-date","title":"Still paid two fiscal years after the end date on record","question":"Which contracts were still being paid long after the end date the contract table shows?","finding":"Hardly any. Of 19,284 contracts that ended between July 2018 and June 2025 and were paid, 92 (0.5%) drew payments two or more fiscal years after their end date, $15.8 million in all; the highest rate is in construction (15 of 884). The table's end date is the present one: when a contract is extended the date is moved, so this test can only find payments that outlived every recorded extension. Read from the fiscal-year label on each payment instead, the count would be 149: the payment file carries some earlier payments under a later year, mostly on purchase orders in multi-year capital funds ($5.52 billion of $119.25 billion, 4.6% of all payments since fiscal 2019, and 9.3% of payments on contracts, carry a later year than their voucher number belongs to).","how":"Each contract's end date in the Supplier Contracts table (as of 2026-11-08) was set against the fiscal years in which it was paid. A payment's year is taken from its voucher number, which is one running sequence: each fiscal year's file holds its own block of numbers plus older numbers filed under it later, and those older payments are counted in the year their number belongs to (fiscal 2018 or earlier for the lowest block). A contract is listed when a fiscal year at least two after the one in which it ended holds payments of $1,000 and 1% of everything paid on it. The year after the end date is not counted, because final invoices and retention are normally paid then.","limits":"A late payment can be retention released at the end of a warranty period, a disputed invoice settled, or a claim paid; on construction contracts that is routine. The end date may simply not have been updated when the contract was extended. Voucher numbers date a payment to a fiscal year only approximately near the turn of each year. This screen cannot see contracts that were extended on the record, which is how most contracts run long: for those the first end date exists only in Board files (the screen above) and in departments' own records.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"contractor","t":"Paid","type":"org"},{"k":"department","t":"Department","type":"text"},{"k":"title","t":"Contract","type":"text"},{"k":"kind","t":"Kind of work","type":"text"},{"k":"end","t":"End date on record","type":"date"},{"k":"ceiling","t":"Ceiling","type":"usd"},{"k":"paid","t":"Paid in all","type":"usd"},{"k":"paidLate","t":"Paid two or more fiscal years after the end","type":"usd"},{"k":"yearsPast","t":"Fiscal years past the end","type":"int"},{"k":"lastPaid","t":"Last fiscal year paid","type":"year"},{"k":"contract","t":"Contract number","type":"text"}],"rows":[{"department":"Mayor","title":"MYR Sunnydale 1A3 Relo & Mega","kind":"grants to nonprofits","end":"2023-12-31","ceiling":4888633,"paid":4867893,"paidLate":4867893,"yearsPast":2,"lastPaid":2026,"contract":"1000030748","contractor":"San Francisco Housing Authority","contractorKey":null},{"department":"City Administrator","title":"Police Vehicles with Upfitting","kind":"goods and general services","end":"2023-01-15","ceiling":9850000,"paid":9389558,"paidLate":1581351,"yearsPast":3,"lastPaid":2026,"contract":"1000016950","contractor":"Bob Wondries Ford/Wondries Fleet Group","contractorKey":null},{"department":"Mayor","title":"MYR Treasure Is E1.2Behavioral","kind":"grants to nonprofits","end":"2024-06-30","ceiling":4679657,"paid":4631839,"paidLate":1474957,"yearsPast":3,"lastPaid":2027,"contract":"1000029993","contractor":"Treasure Island E1.2 Behavioral Health L","contractorKey":null},{"department":"Public Utilities Commission","title":"PUC SF Loc Wtr AsNeeded Pave","kind":"construction","end":"2021-06-30","ceiling":37187430,"paid":21726397,"paidLate":1027400,"yearsPast":2,"lastPaid":2023,"contract":"1000000618","contractor":"A Ruiz Construction Co And As